  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Indonesia continues to manage widespread flooding incidents across several provinces, affecting thousands of residents. Recent reports indicate that 16 villages in Pidie Jaya, Aceh, are currently submerged, while North Sumatra faces significant impacts with over a thousand households affected in areas such as Padang Lawas Utara. In response, authorities have established temporary relief facilities, including community kitchens in Bengkulu, and are managing the transition of flood survivors in Aceh Tamiang into permanent housing. Infrastructure remains a key focus, with ongoing efforts by the Ministry of Public Works to restore road access in Gayo Lues and Takengon. Meanwhile, in urban centers like Surabaya and Jakarta, local officials and legislative bodies are accelerating drainage and pump station projects to address rising water levels and tidal flooding, reflecting a broad effort to combat the ongoing hydrometeorological challenges across the archipelago.",
